twistr is an independent, from-scratch reimplementation with a different
architecture (asynchronous rather than threaded), and its own scanning,
scoring, and output logic. Portions studied from dnstwist and adapted for
use here include:

  * the keyboard-adjacency maps used by the typo fuzzers,
  * the homoglyph substitution method and part of its glyph data, and
  * the per-registry IDN character tables.

These portions have been modified and integrated into a new codebase. No
endorsement by the dnstwist project or its author is claimed or implied.
